### Parliamentary questions

questions:QuestionOralWork 
  sh:description "Parliamentary questions for oral answer dealt with during plenary sittings, and included in the day's debates. They may be followed by a resolution (Rule 142). Also includes Questions for Question Time asked during the period set aside for questions during plenary sittings (Rule 143)."@en ;
  as:agentInstruction "An MEP may ask multiple questions during a sitting"@en ;
.

questions:P43 sh:path epvoc:workHadParticipation;
  sh:description "Links an oral question to the participation entry that describes the stakeholders of this question (in particular its author)"@en;
.

questions:P33 sh:path dcterms:title ;
  sh:agentInstruction "Titles are multilingual in every EU official language. If you need a title, filter them in a single language depending on user preference."@en ;
.

questions:QuestionWrittenWork
  sh:description "Written parliamentary questions with a request for a written answer (Rule 144)"@en ;
  as:agentInstruction "An MEP may ask multiple questions during a sitting"@en ;
.

questions:P24 sh:path epvoc:workHadParticipation;
  sh:description "Links a written question to the participation entry that describes the stakeholders of this question (in particular its author)"@en;
.

questions:P14 sh:path dcterms:title ;
  sh:agentInstruction "Titles are multilingual in every EU official language. If you need a title, filter them in a single language depending on user preference."@en ;
.

questions:InterpellationMajorWork
  sh:description "Major interpellations may be tabled by a political group to the Council, the Commission or the Vice-President of the Commission/High-Representative of the Union for Foreign Affairs and Security Policy."@en ;
  as:agentInstruction "An MEP may issue multiple interpellation on the same day"@en ;
.

questions:P61 sh:path epvoc:workHadParticipation;
  sh:description "Links a major interpellation to the participation entry that describes the stakeholders of this question (in particular its author)"@en;
.

questions:P51 sh:path dcterms:title ;
  sh:agentInstruction "Titles are multilingual in every EU official language. If you need a title, filter them in a single language depending on user preference."@en ;
.

questions:Participation 
  sh:description "Describes the participation of stakeholders (participants) with respect to a document. Particpants may be persons or organizations. Participants plays a role (in particular, the role of authors of documents). Persons can participate in the name of an organization."@en ;
.

questions:P133 sh:path eli-dl:participation_role;
  sh:agentInstruction "Use <https://data.europarl.europa.eu/def/ep-roles/AUTHOR> for authors and <https://data.europarl.europa.eu/def/ep-roles/ADDRESSEE> for addressees of questions."
.

questions:WorkTypeReference
  sh:agentInstruction "This is a SKOS concept with a skos:prefLabel"@en ;
.

### Meetings

mtg:Activity-GMTG-PL
  sh:description "The European Parliament plenary part-session shall be the meeting of the Europeal Parliament convened as a rule each month and subdivided into daily sittings."@en
.

mtg:Activity-MTG-PL 
  sh:description "The European Parliament plenary sitting is a subdivision of a plenary part-session. Sittings of the Parliament held on the same day shall be deemed to be a single sitting."@en ;
.

mtg:P34 sh:path eli-dl:had_participant_person;
    sh:description "Relates a sitting to an MEP that participated in this sitting."@en;
.

mtg:ActivityType-Node
  sh:agentInstruction "This is a SKOS concept with a skos:prefLabel"@en ;
.